[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ### Step 2: Use known formulas for inradius and circumradius
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m We know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $R = 13$ (circumradius)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $r = 6$ (inradius)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m We are to find $AB \cdot AC$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $AB = c$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $AC = b$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $BC = a$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - Then $AB \cdot AC = bc$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m We also know that in a triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m r = \frac{A}{s}
