[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ### Step 5: Use the formula for the distance between incenter and circumcenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m There is a known formula for the distance $OI$ between the incenter and circumcenter:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m OI^2 = R(R - 2r)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m This is a well-known formula in triangle geometry.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m OI^2 = R(R - 2r) = 13(13 - 2 \cdot 6) = 13(13 - 12) = 13 \cdot 1 = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m OI = \sqrt{13}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ### Step 6: Use the Pythagorean theorem in triangle $IAO$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m We are told that $\overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI}$, so triangle $IAO$ is a right triangle with:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $IA$ perpendicular to $OI$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $OI = \sqrt{13}$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $AO = R = 13$ (since the circumradius is 13),
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m IA^2 + OI^2 = AO^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m \Rightarrow IA^2 + 13 = 13^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m \Rightarrow IA^2 = 13^2 - 13 = 169 - 13 = 156
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m \Rightarrow IA = \sqrt{156} = 2\sqrt{39}
