[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ### Step 5: Consider the interval $ [1, 3) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m In this interval, $ f(x) = 2 - x $, which is **positive** for $ x \in [1, 2) $ and **negative** for $ x \in [2, 3) $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So, we can split this into two subintervals:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m #### Case 1: $ x \in [1, 2) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Here, $ f(x) = 2 - x $, and we are looking for $ f(x) = \sqrt{\frac{x}{34}} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 2 - x = \sqrt{\frac{x}{34}} \quad \text{for } x \in [1, 2)
