[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So $OI = \sqrt{13}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m We also know that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m IA \perp OI \Rightarrow \text{The angle between } \vec{IA} \text{ and } \vec{OI} \text{ is } 90^\circ
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So the vectors are perpendicular.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Let’s use the fact that in a triangle, the distance from the incenter to a vertex can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m IA = \sqrt{r^2 + (s - a)^2}
