[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - $ d $ divides 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So, we find all divisors of 56 that are greater than 10.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m The divisors of 56 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Now, the ones greater than 10 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So, the possible values of $ d = b + 7 $ are 14, 28, 56.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - If $ d = 14 $, then $ b = 14 - 7 = 7 $ → but $ b > 9 $, so this is invalid.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - If $ d = 28 $, then $ b = 28 - 7 = 21 $ → valid.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - If $ d = 56 $, then $ b = 56 - 7 = 49 $ → valid.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So the valid values of $ b $ are 21 and 49.
