[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Geometry of the Rhombus
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m In a rhombus, the diagonals are perpendicular and bisect each other. Since the diagonals intersect at the origin, we can assume the diagonals are along the coordinate axes. Let the diagonals be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
