[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - 4 hours = 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - 2 hours and 24 minutes = 2 + 24/60 = 2.4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Let’s denote the time spent walking as $ t_w $, and the time spent in the coffee shop as $ t_c = 3 $ minutes = $ \frac{3}{60} = 0.05 $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So, the total time for each scenario is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - At speed $ s $: $ t_w + t_c = 4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m - At speed $ s + 2 $: $ t_w + t_c = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m Let’s denote the time taken to walk 9 kilometers at speed $ s $ as $ t_w $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m So, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25285)[0m \frac{9}{s} = t_w \quad \text{(1)}
